<!-- OTHER POLLUTANTS -->
<section id="pollutants">
    <h2>Other Gases Released by Burning Fossil Fuels</h2>
    <div class="flex-row">
        <div class="flex-col">
            <p>
                Burning fossil fuels also releases harmful pollutants that are not greenhouse gases but still 
                damage health and the environment.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Sulfur dioxide (SO₂):</strong> Causes acid rain; damages plants and buildings.</li>
                <li><strong>Nitrogen oxides (NOₓ):</strong> Contribute to smog and acid rain; irritate lungs.</li>
                <li><strong>Particulates (PM2.5/PM10):</strong> Tiny particles that cause respiratory and heart problems.</li>
                <li><strong>Carbon monoxide (CO):</strong> Toxic gas that reduces oxygen transport in blood.</li>
                <li><strong>Unburnt hydrocarbons:</strong> Contribute to ground‑level ozone formation.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
